# ONNX Runtime as every package carries it (the handwriting search loads it at run time: qt/src/hwr/OrtRuntime.cpp).
# Read by qt/scripts/onnxruntime-fetch.sh, which downloads, checks and unpacks it for one platform.
#
# Bumping it is this one file: the version, then the sha256 of each file below (download them and run sha256sum on
# them; GitHub also shows the digest on the release page). The app needs C API version 16 or newer (1.16+); the
# headers in qt/3rdparty/onnxruntime are 1.30.0 (C API 30). Linux: the library's newest GLIBC_ symbol must exist on
# Ubuntu 22.04 (glibc 2.35): `objdump -T libonnxruntime.so.1.* | grep -o 'GLIBC_[0-9.]*' | sort -uV | tail -1`
# (1.30.0: GLIBC_2.28, GLIBCXX_3.4.22). See qt/docs/development/releasing.md, "Handwriting: ONNX Runtime and the model".
#
# Plain shell assignments (sourced by bash; no spaces around =).

XQT_ORT_VERSION=1.30.0

# Microsoft's release archives (https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/releases)
XQT_ORT_LINUX_X64_SHA256=a5ed5a3cac51fbb2e90da632ae43d19212faaa20e76484e62bcb7c23ddb3b3fd
XQT_ORT_WIN_X64_SHA256=c6ba983baf5681af108599675d2a89c2d145512d02de28aed0bff177cd0ba949
XQT_ORT_OSX_ARM64_SHA256=6ebb5062a934537c352937821f9fe9718e7de1a2db1122a93dd363ffd53a7012

# Android: the AAR from Maven Central (com.microsoft.onnxruntime:onnxruntime-android); it has no licence files, so
# LICENSE and ThirdPartyNotices.txt come from the release's tag (the same files as in the archives above)
XQT_ORT_ANDROID_AAR_SHA256=e7fb945e402205f6db858d65bb78d2bdb0812317b383976c9e3bceb4862c73f1
XQT_ORT_LICENSE_SHA256=2f07c72751aed99790b8a4869cf2311df85a860b22ded05fa22803587a48922c
XQT_ORT_NOTICES_SHA256=143764b952fdb1a7c69ce653bfba74a7744d6a8a573bfb73e235fba356c83de3
